    this.roundMap.set('AA.Qen00062',',AA.Qen00062,Ed-U-Games tm,20070808,10,ThWrLe,Hi16 HiNoNoUS,,PoCo PoUS CiUS,us founding documents;bill of rights;declaration of independence;the constitution;treaty of alliance;treaty of paris;,,aPRA1_179 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,Answer these questions about US Founding Documents.,,Rows=4 Cols=1 FntSize=10 FntColor=black BkGndColor=white LnCnt=5 SingleScreen=No Sort=No ,AnswerType=RowsOfButtons AnsRows=5 AnsCols=1 AnsLnCnt=1 AnsFntSize=24 AnsFntColor=black AnsBkGndColor=green Answers=Bill of Rights;Declaration of Independence;The Constitution;Treaty of Alliance;Treaty of Paris; ,Which document contains the words Governments are instituted among Men: deriving their just Powers from the Consent of the governed..; ;Declaration of Independence,The wording Congress shall make no law respecting an establishment of religion: or prohibiting the free exercise thereof: or abridging the freedom of speech: or of the press: or the right of the people peaceably to assemble: and to petition the government for a redress of grievances.  is part of what document?;Amendment I: Congress shall make no law respecting an establishment of religion: or prohibiting the free exercise thereof: or abridging the freedom of speech: or of the press: or the right of the people peaceably to assemble: and to petition the government for a redress of grievances.;Bill of Rights,The right to be informed of the nature and cause of the accusation is part of what document?;Amendment VI:  In all criminal prosecutions: the accused shall enjoy the right to a speedy and public trial: by an impartial jury of the state and district wherein the crime shall have been committed: which district shall have been previously ascertained by law: and to be informed of the nature and cause of the accusation: to be confronted with the witnesses against him: to have compulsory process for obtaining witnesses in his favor: and to have the assistance of counsel for his defense.;Bill of Rights,Which document was signed on 6 Feb 1778?; ;Treaty of Alliance,Which Document was originally composed and concluded in the French Language?; ;Treaty of Alliance,The Bill of Rights are amendments to what document?; ;The Constitution,Which document declared peace with Great Britain?;The Treaty of Paris was signed on Sept. 3: 1783.  It declared peace between Great Britain and the new country of the United States. Great Britain recognized the independence of the American colonies.;Treaty of Paris,Which was the second document signed in Paris?; ;Treaty of Paris,Which document starts with In the name of the most holy and undivided Trinity.; ;Treaty of Paris');
